<%# Credits as ambient status, not a line of reading: a bolt and a number in the
    top-right corner, the Duolingo-gems / Midjourney-fast-hours pattern. It was a
    full-width row under the intro, which put a price tag in the middle of the
    screen's first paragraph.

    This is now the only credits pill in the app: Home's header used to carry one
    too, and it was removed — a balance belongs on the screen that spends it. The
    styling is inherited from that pill, one step larger, since here it stands
    alone against a 30px title and the number is also the tap target.

    The digit alone is the whole label, so the reading of it lives in aria-label.
    `justify-between` in the header row puts this top-right in LTR and top-left
    under dir="rtl", which is where a corner badge belongs in each.

    Links to the Pro paywall. It used to link to /app/credits, the sheet that
    sold consumable packs; credits are no longer purchasable, so the only thing
    a tap on the meter can offer is the subscription that removes it. %>
<%= link_to app_pro_path,
            id: "credits-pill",
            class: "shrink-0 flex items-center gap-1.5 bg-app-pill rounded-full py-2 px-3.5",
            aria: { label: "#{t('app.import_requests.index.credits_remaining', credits: balance)}. #{t('app.import_requests.index.credits_add')}" } do %>
  <%= app_icon "bolt", class: "w-4 h-4 text-app-accent" %>
  <span class="text-app-credits text-[15px] font-bold leading-none"><%= balance %></span>
<% end %>
